{"chapter": "sets", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "000F", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\phi(x_1, x_2) = \\exists x (x\\in x_1 \\wedge x\\in x_2)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\phi^M(x_1, x_2) = \\exists x \\in M (x\\in x_1 \\wedge x\\in x_2)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": " "}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:81c63a52363185547bf491bc69893591916e055c75e550df61b7b3b869e48db4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:eff894f31c4066f086d7648d8e17fb628a8ffe9f877780869a8c4c2dfde6809e", "source_text": "So the formula <MATH_0001> is turned into <MATH_0002>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7f29903112b782869d6895cb1b5fc9b5c4b2f9672031fa35176e3a43da6a788d", "unit_id": "tag:000F:p003"}
{"chapter": "sets", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "000F", "placeholders": {"EMPHCLOSE_0001": "}", "EMPHOPEN_0001": "\\emph{", "MATH_0001": "$\\phi^M$", "MATH_0002": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0003": "$M$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3c520b56f25aa2a6401dcdee29e8c2e57a958c4ffa39500e4e31147efeb25608", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f83cadfa76d32eb6561244c1085034a41206ca2719682fdab11a58aafca9e6e1", "source_text": "The formula <MATH_0001> is called the <EMPHOPEN_0001>relativization of <MATH_0002> to <MATH_0003><EMPHCLOSE_0001>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d1b0771db8ab1653362da3f0e0f6ee347d307fef405d2cb0b5070850b1a92f76", "unit_id": "tag:000F:p004"}
{"chapter": "sets", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "000G", "placeholders": {"BOLDCLOSE_0001": "}", "BOLDOPEN_0001": "{\\bf ", "MATH_0001": "$\\phi_1(x_1, \\ldots, x_n), \\ldots, \\phi_m(x_1, \\ldots, x_n)$", "MATH_0002": "$M_0$", "MATH_0003": "$M$", "MATH_0004": "$M_0 \\subset M$", "MATH_0005": "$\\forall x_1, \\ldots, x_n \\in M$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\forall i = 1, \\ldots, m, \\ \\phi_i^{M}(x_1, \\ldots, x_n)\n\\Leftrightarrow\n\\forall i = 1, \\ldots, m, \\ \\phi_i(x_1, \\ldots, x_n).\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$M = V_\\alpha$", "MATH_0008": "$\\alpha$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{sets-theorem-reflection-principle}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{theorem}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0a5a57621e4dac3d1287390588e24f9db97ccb15ceeb5959c043388ac5a24a7c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d92ec348692d205930193421207c7df313058f36e4d6042ec03192a3f92d8cdb", "source_text": "Suppose given <MATH_0001> a <BOLDOPEN_0001>finite<BOLDCLOSE_0001> collection of formulas of set theory. Let <MATH_0002> be a set. There exists a set <MATH_0003> such that <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005>, we have <MATH_0006> In fact we may take <MATH_0007> for some limit ordinal <MATH_0008>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:98b925e05b4dfc63a7e4d2d703df5bcdcd1f4395ac1cfa536f15b587c526507f", "unit_id": "tag:000G"}
{"chapter": "sets", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "000G", "placeholders": {"CITE_0001": "\\cite[Theorem 12.14]{Jech}", "CITE_0002": "\\cite[Theorem 7.4]{Kunen}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{proof}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:759c2566837a2b904d8428f7ac2373e524142dd52555474474f9e33c5e05e7b6", "source_text": "See <CITE_0001> or <CITE_0002>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:11ecf2d744ad3c9afae45838aab929443aea63b7a7426ae60ec76cc1d2cc43fd", "unit_id": "tag:000G:proof-p001"}
{"chapter": "sets", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "000F", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$x_1, \\ldots, x_n \\in M$", "MATH_0002": "$V_\\alpha$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\noindent\n", "suffix": " "}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:15c37f7640a68f0860205cd035015caafe037f1455c690905b817ff5f1f2ad99", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cca09b609d5e792e38b883daea397dc7228f8edd4217414ad54c10f6f13cf2b2", "source_text": "We view this theorem as saying the following: Given any <MATH_0001> the formulas hold with the bound variables ranging through all sets if and only if they hold for the bound variables ranging through elements of <MATH_0002>. This theorem is a meta-theorem because it deals with the formulas of set theory directly.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0995a622de10cf58593066775d50c6a47107606e5cf3a39a14c728e15ee425aa", "unit_id": "tag:000F:p005"}
{"chapter": "sets", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "000F", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\phi_1, \\ldots, \\phi_m$", "MATH_0002": "$x_1, \\ldots, x_n$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\forall M_0\\ \\exists M, \\ M_0 \\subset M\\ \\forall x_1, \\ldots, x_n \\in M \\\\\n\\phi_1(x_1, \\ldots, x_n) \\wedge \\ldots \\wedge \\phi_m(x_1, \\ldots, x_n)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\phi_1^M(x_1, \\ldots, x_n) \\wedge \\ldots \\wedge \\phi_m^M(x_1, \\ldots, x_n)\n\\end{matrix}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$\\phi_i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:398749aa239456b0a035cb520aadebde7628de07ba3214106617269c94b83a4c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:299ba80cfe2f7343248ef6e0fe66d222cd7f64c891bb3fad088b538b430a4409", "source_text": "It actually says that given the finite list of formulas <MATH_0001> with at most free variables <MATH_0002> the sentence <MATH_0003> is provable in ZFC. In other words, whenever we actually write down a finite list of formulas <MATH_0004>, we get a theorem.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6b500f91751f28c6c9b931403164a8fc8f7f650791cc719ce096840db434df2a", "unit_id": "tag:000F:p006"}
{"chapter": "sets", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "000F", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\phi_i^M(x_1, \\ldots, x_n)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\medskip\\noindent\n", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:aafab7d357b10b7ffb9a33170f18af5da391949c9e720fb48d96741302565b18", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0c07048dfeeb0e9c57af78f931e7108037ac36d725788c2001d2920ead0047b1", "source_text": "It is somewhat hard to use this theorem in ``ordinary mathematics'' since the meaning of the formulas <MATH_0001> is not so clear! Instead, we will use the idea of the proof of the reflection principle to prove the existence results we need directly.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:11ebd30351ad6711890da6316c294b6da6e228af8297afdb93c4fd5d12b1b247", "unit_id": "tag:000F:p007"}
